    "annotation": "Downstream multivariable association analysis of amplicon sequencing data starting from an ASV/OTU phyloseq object. The workflow includes sequencing-control assessment, contaminant identification and removal based on negative control samples, visualization and assessment of positive control samples, batch-effect correction, normalization, feature filtering, and multivariable association and differential abundance analysis. Analyses can be performed at the ASV/OTU level or on features aggregated to different taxonomic levels. The workflow supports the incorporation of multiple fixed and random effects, continuous and categorical metadata variables, and relevant covariates to account for potential confounding factors and repeated or correlated measurements. Users can select appropriate normalization and transformation strategies and statistical models, enabling the identification of microbial features associated with biological or experimental variables of interest while accounting for complex study designs.",
