        {
            "color": "none",
            "data": {
                "text": "## 6. Taxonomic-level differential abundance analysis\n\nPhyloseq object is taxonomically agglomerated before a second MaAsLin3 analysis."
            },
            "id": 11,
            "position": [
                8286.9,
                438
            ],
            "size": [
                570,
                110
            ],
            "type": "markdown"
        },
        {
            "color": "none",
            "data": {
                "text": "## 5. Differential abundance analysis\n\nMaAsLin3 tests multivariable associations between microbial features and sample metadata using the user-defined model formula and reference level."
            },
            "id": 9,
            "position": [
                7225.1,
                788.6
            ],
            "size": [
                560,
                115
            ],
            "type": "markdown"
        },
        {
            "color": "none",
            "data": {
                "text": "## 4. Batch-effect correction and phyloseq reconstruction\n\nBatch effects in ASV abundances are corrected using MMUPHin. The corrected abundance table is then reformatted and combined with taxonomy and metadata to reconstruct a corrected phyloseq object for downstream taxonomic analysis."
            },
            "id": 7,
            "position": [
                6379.2,
                109.19999999999999
            ],
            "size": [
                650,
                125
            ],
            "type": "markdown"
        },
        {
            "color": "none",
            "data": {
                "text": "## 3. Decontamination\n\nPotential contaminant ASVs are identified using negative sequencing controls. Sequencing-control samples are removed before downstream analyses."
            },
            "id": 5,
            "position": [
                4482.7,
                0
            ],
            "size": [
                560,
                110
            ],
            "type": "markdown"
        },
        {
            "color": "none",
            "data": {
                "text": "## 2. Sequencing control assessment\n\nNegative and positive sequencing controls are identified from the sample metadata and visualised to assess potential contamination before decontamination."
            },
            "id": 2,
            "position": [
                3273.2,
                458.5000000000001
            ],
            "size": [
                520,
                110
            ],
            "type": "markdown"
        }
    ],
